@startuml
' =============================================================================
' Converse tool-use loop — UML sequence diagram
'
' Mermaid source set : diagrams/mermaid/04-converse-api-application.md (view C)
' Chapter            : 01-amazon-bedrock/inference/01-converse-api.md
' Verified           : 2026-11-15
' Status             : academy design, not an official AWS reference architecture.
'                      No AWS icons; nothing is included from the network.
'
' Official sources this view relies on:
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/conversation-inference.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_ConverseStream.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/tool-use.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/tool-use-client-side.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_ToolUseBlockStart.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_runtime_ToolResultBlock.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-api-error-codes.html
'
' What UML adds over the Mermaid view: the tool rounds are an explicit loop
' fragment with its exit condition, and the stop reasons are alternatives.
' =============================================================================
!pragma layout smetana
title Converse tool-use loop — one user turn with ConverseStream (UML sequence)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #666666
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #888888

autonumber
box "Internet — untrusted" #F1F3F4
  actor "Client" as U #E8F1FB
end box
box "Your AWS account · one Region" #FFFBF5
  participant "Chat service\nexecution role · tool loop" as A #FDEBD0
  database "Amazon DynamoDB\nconversation history" as H #EDE7F6
  participant "Tool implementation\nleast-privilege role per tool" as T #FDEBD0
end box
box "AWS-managed service boundary · Amazon Bedrock" #F5FBF6
  participant "Amazon Bedrock Runtime\nConverseStream" as B #E6F4EA
end box

U -> A : User message for a session
note over U, A : User authenticated at the entry point
A -> H : Load the messages of the session
H --> A : Message list

loop Tool rounds — until stopReason is not tool_use; cap the number of rounds per turn
  A -> B : ConverseStream with system, full history, toolConfig\n(after round 1: plus the assistant toolUse and user toolResult messages)
  note over A, B : SigV4 with the execution role · IAM bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream\nBedrock stores nothing between calls: every call carries the whole history
  opt Throttled before the stream starts
    B --> A : 429 ThrottlingException
    A -> B : Retry with backoff · bounded attempts
  end
  B --> A : messageStart, then contentBlockDelta text events
  A --> U : Forward text deltas as they arrive
  alt stopReason tool_use
    B --> A : toolUse block events, then messageStop with stopReason tool_use
    note right of A : Assemble the toolUse block from contentBlockStart\n(toolUseId, name) and the partial JSON in the deltas.\nSeveral toolUse blocks: one toolResult per toolUseId,\nall in a single user message
    A -> T : Run the tool with the parsed input
    T --> A : Result or error
    note right of A : On a tool error, return a toolResult with\nstatus error and a short message — never drop it
  else stopReason end_turn
    B --> A : Text deltas, then messageStop with stopReason end_turn, then metadata with usage
    A --> U : Forward the rest of the answer
  end
end

A -> H : Append the user, assistant and tool messages
opt Error event after partial output
  B --> A : modelStreamErrorException in the stream
  A --> U : Mark the answer incomplete and offer a retry
  note right of A : Do not restart silently and duplicate output.\nDo not save a half-finished assistant message as complete
end

note across
  Other stop reasons — max_tokens: the answer is truncated · guardrail_intervened: show the guardrail's message ·
  model_context_window_exceeded: trim or summarize the history before retrying (the exact semantics of this value are our reading).
  The model never runs a tool itself: it returns a toolUse request and your code runs the tool.
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | solid arrow | request or call |
  | dashed arrow | response, or an event on the open stream |
  | loop / alt / opt | repetition, alternatives, optional step |
  |<#F1F3F4> grey box | outside your AWS account |
  |<#FDEBD0> orange | your compute |
  |<#EDE7F6> purple | data at rest |
  |<#E6F4EA> green | Amazon Bedrock |
  Academy design · not an official AWS diagram · Verified 2026-11-15
endlegend
@enduml
